      "heading": "21 to 99",
      "body": "21–29 are written as one word: *veintiuno, veintidós, veintitrés, veinticuatro, veinticinco, veintiséis, veintisiete, veintiocho, veintinueve*. From 31 on, use *y* (and): *treinta y uno, cuarenta y cinco, noventa y nueve*.",
      "table": {
        "head": ["Tens", "", "Tens", ""],
        "rows": [
          ["30", "*treinta*", "70", "*setenta*"],
          ["40", "*cuarenta*", "80", "*ochenta*"],
          ["50", "*cincuenta*", "90", "*noventa*"],
          ["60", "*sesenta*", "100", "*cien*"]
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "heading": "100 and up",
      "body": "*Cien* is exactly 100; from 101 it becomes *ciento*: *ciento uno, ciento cincuenta*. The hundreds agree with feminine nouns: *doscientos pesos*, *doscientas personas*.\n\n200 *doscientos* · 300 *trescientos* · 400 *cuatrocientos* · 500 *quinientos* · 600 *seiscientos* · 700 *setecientos* · 800 *ochocientos* · 900 *novecientos* · 1,000 *mil* · 2,000 *dos mil* · 1,000,000 *un millón*.\n\nNote: no *y* between hundreds and tens (*ciento veinte*, not \"ciento y veinte\"), and *mil* never takes *un* (*mil pesos*). Many Latin American countries write 1,000 as *1.000* and use a comma for decimals."
    },
    {
      "heading": "How much is it?",
      "body": "- *¿Cuánto cuesta?* — How much does it cost? (one thing)\n- *¿Cuánto cuestan?* — How much do they cost?\n- *¿Cuánto es?* — How much is it (all together)?\n- *Cuesta veinte pesos.* — It costs twenty pesos.\n\nCurrencies vary: *el peso* (Mexico, Colombia, Argentina, Chile…), *el sol* (Peru), *el dólar* (Ecuador, El Salvador, the US). *Es caro* (it's expensive), *es barato* (it's cheap)."
    }
